# twin: render_two
# Two consoles that draw the two-part picture in Vulkan, each parked inside
# its frames between the parts while the other draws. Console 0's core
# makes its instance and device through a version 2 negotiation interface
# and hands part 1's command buffer over for the frontend to submit;
# console 1's makes its device through a version 1 one and passes the
# picture with semaphores both ways. Console 1 passes no picture in frames
# 100 to 110: the semaphore it set for each of those frames must still be
# signalled, or its next frame waits on one nothing signals.
console 0 core=test render=vulkan
console 1 core=test render=vulkan
option 0 link_test_render vulkan
option 0 link_test_vk_negotiate v2
option 0 link_test_vk_handoff commands
option 0 link_test_seed 3
option 0 link_test_steps 16
option 0 link_test_lookahead_0 1
option 1 link_test_render vulkan
option 1 link_test_vk_negotiate v1
option 1 link_test_vk_handoff semaphore
option 1 link_test_seed 7
option 1 link_test_steps 16
option 1 link_test_lookahead_0 1
option 1 link_test_dupe_frames 100-110
0 cable 0:0 1:0
60 save mid
60 checkpoint in_flight
100 checkpoint before
101 checkpoint dupe
200 end
